WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.770
NARRATOR: Badlands National
Park, South Dakota,

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:16.900
244,000 acres split into two
dramatic worlds, the Rocky

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:25.436
Badlands themselves, carved out
of the ground by wind and rain,

00:00:25.436 --> 00:00:32.229
and beyond them, an
ancient sea of grass,

00:00:32.229 --> 00:00:37.810
home to the icons
of the Old West.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.420
This land has a long
and deep connection

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.600
to the indigenous
peoples of America.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.150
It's the current
and traditional land

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.810
of the Oglala Lakota tribe.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:55.880
For 12,000 years, people
have used these lands,

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.760
but prairie dogs have
been here even longer.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.239
A female black-tailed
prairie dog

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:09.470
lives on the
grasslands in a family

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:12.185
group known as a coterie.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.110
In spring it's time for
her to start a family.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.860
After mating, she
maintains her burrow

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.450
and collects nesting material.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.405
In doing so, she
becomes an ecoengineer.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:56.620
Her constant gardening
benefits over 100 species.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:07.320
In the sprawling sea of
grass, the prairie dog town

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:16.380
is an island of life, drawing
in species from far and wide,

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.030
including predators.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.485
Prairie dogs are the perfect
snack for the coyote.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.130
The female's quest
to start a family

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.455
could be over before it started.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.695
She's completely
oblivious to the threat.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.715
However, the prairie
dog has allies.

00:03:03.715 --> 00:03:06.120
[CHIRPING]

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.520
Her neighbors are on high alert.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.432
[CHIRPING]

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:22.052
Each prairie dog town comes with
its own built-in alarm system.

00:03:22.052 --> 00:03:23.990
[CHIRPING]

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.000
It's one of the
most complex animal

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.410
languages ever decoded,
with specific calls

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.715
for different threats.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.040
The coyote is spotted.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.750
And short chirps call him out.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.405
[CHIRPING]

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.895
He literally has
nowhere to hide.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.805
With the threat gone, they
give the all clear signal--

00:03:52.805 --> 00:03:55.940
[YIPPING]

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:56.990
--a jump yip.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.410
The key to thriving
in the badlands

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:11.130
is looking out for each other.

